# Names of the environment variables the pipeline expects.
# No values here: copy this file to .env and fill it in locally, or export the
# variables in your shell. .env is ignored by git and read at startup by the
# pipeline itself; a variable already exported always wins over the file.
#
# Only secrets live here. Everything else — which model writes, which endpoint it
# calls, how many items the digest keeps — is configuration, and lives in the TOML
# files under config/.

# --- Triage (stage 3) ---
# TypeSafe key, from https://console.typesafe.ai/settings/keys.
# Nothing else is needed: the API base URL and the model name have working defaults
# (`https://api.typesafe.ai` and `jev-latest`). The SDK also honours
# TYPESAFE_BASE_URL, TYPESAFE_DEFAULT_MODEL and TYPESAFE_LOG_LEVEL in the shell, if
# you ever need to override them for one run.
TYPESAFE_API_KEY=

# --- Writing (stage 4) ---
# OpenRouter key, from https://openrouter.ai/keys. The writer model, its endpoint and
# the digest size are set in config/write.toml, where the three compared models and
# their monthly cost are listed.
WRITE_LLM_API_KEY=
